DESIGN_FP_ARCH_CH.md:536:**Debts and favours (proposal 6).** RN regard incidents with typed reasons (`ransomed_by`, `paid_well`, `sheltered`, `betrayed`, `refused_at_gate`, `slandered`), owned by RN's closed reason vocabulary; a favour owed is a warm link with its reason, called in when the creditor court's offer weighs it (§7). CH'S REGISTRATION ROW — the three causes RN's `REGARD_CAUSES` lacked, appended by RN through this row ("PT/CH append rows by registration only", RN §2.4; RN's lane), each with its ONE door, holder and subject, written through RN's one regard writer only: `paid_well` — holder the paragon (`p:<wnpc>`; a corps `u:<unitKey>`), subject the employing court (`c:<court>`), written ONCE by CH's retainer leaf at an `accepted` `retainer_offer` verdict whose `termsBand` is `handsome` or `princely` (keyed by the engagement id, exact-once; DRAFT magnitude, UNMEASURED) — the favour a later offer from that court weighs (§7); `sheltered` — holder the paragon (or a free corps), subject the court of a member town that ADMITS it under its crown's ban (§11's harbouring), written ONCE by CH-5's harbouring write in the same act as its `fealty_defied` row (keyed by that row's `episodeId`, exact-once) — the town that took it in when its crown had barred it; `slandered` — holder the paragon, subject the LIAR court (`liarId`) of an IN lie that named the paragon as a hidden hand (the faked trail, §9), written when IN's landed blowback on the liar fires — DARK until IN's lie family reopens `LURE_AXES` `employer` (SLOT C1, `infoStatecraftEnabled`, lit nowhere), so until then nothing writes it and the word is registered for that door alone. `sheltered` is a HOMONYM of the landed `defensiveTerrain` band (§2.3's P5 row): the cause never prints bare — "Ashford gave her shelter when Merewick's crown had barred her". `ransomed_by` and `betrayed` are RN's own rows and doors (RN's half of WC-RN-50, routed) [CURED 2026-10-20 (fp-final P5) — P5C-14 (WC-RN-50's CH half; `briefs/RULINGS-P5.md` C.14: "RN's `REGARD_CAUSES` appends CH's `paid_well · sheltered · slandered` through CH's registration row (RN's lane; CH cites)"): the three were named "owned by RN's closed reason vocabulary" while RN listed none of them and RN's §14 normalizer drops an unknown cause]. [REFINED 2026-10-17 (fp-final) — WC's "cost memory" is not a carrier (zero symbols; it landed only as `contributionLedger.js`, a court-to-court war-contribution record that "WRITES NOTHING"); RF-10.]
